WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.980 --> 00:00:08.910
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:43.230
This is about the felt
feeling of collectivity

00:00:43.230 --> 00:00:45.150
or the sort of shared feeling.

00:00:47.940 --> 00:00:49.920
This is about something
bigger than just

00:00:49.920 --> 00:00:52.050
being in that space,
looking at this work of art.

00:00:58.840 --> 00:01:02.890
When you see water falling,
you also see time passing.

00:01:02.890 --> 00:01:04.810
And when you see
time passing, you

00:01:04.810 --> 00:01:06.590
see a different kind of space.

00:01:06.590 --> 00:01:11.770
What a waterfall can do is add
an element of temporal quality,

00:01:11.770 --> 00:01:14.680
an element of
inclusivity, an element

00:01:14.680 --> 00:01:18.565
for a possibility to share an
experience, a shared space.

00:01:18.565 --> 00:01:21.808
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:01:36.770 --> 00:01:39.290
It's a great thing if
you can somehow combine

00:01:39.290 --> 00:01:40.535
singularity and collectivity.

00:01:40.535 --> 00:01:43.832
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:01:52.610 --> 00:01:54.770
The presence of other
people in the piece

00:01:54.770 --> 00:01:57.208
plays a central role
for your experience.

00:02:00.630 --> 00:02:05.480
What is it that makes a space
challenging, and exciting,

00:02:05.480 --> 00:02:09.740
and embracing, and including,
and hospitable, and intolerant,

00:02:09.740 --> 00:02:10.280
and so on?

00:02:10.280 --> 00:02:11.000
What is that?

00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:14.472
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:03:09.050 --> 00:03:12.050
About 10 years ago, I had an
exhibition here at the Tate

00:03:12.050 --> 00:03:13.680
called The Weather
Project, where

00:03:13.680 --> 00:03:17.420
I had something like a very
big sun in the Turbine Hall.

00:03:17.420 --> 00:03:20.240
It also became about the
people which were in the space,

00:03:20.240 --> 00:03:25.055
and about the feeling
of being in that space.

00:03:25.055 --> 00:03:27.140
I've now for a
while been working

00:03:27.140 --> 00:03:29.360
on an idea for a
work of art, which

00:03:29.360 --> 00:03:32.030
is this little thing here.

00:03:32.030 --> 00:03:33.200
I call it Little Sun.

00:03:33.200 --> 00:03:36.644
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:03:46.976 --> 00:03:51.980
A solar panel, a container,
light on the other side.

00:03:51.980 --> 00:03:53.180
I charge it.

00:03:53.180 --> 00:03:56.540
Four hours of charging gives
you five hours of light.

00:04:00.050 --> 00:04:01.550
Most people who
don't have energy,

00:04:01.550 --> 00:04:05.120
they rely on kerosene
for lighting.

00:04:05.120 --> 00:04:08.000
Kerosene, of course,
is unhealthy.

00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:12.970
This one is 10 times
cheaper than kerosene.

00:04:12.970 --> 00:04:17.480
It has 10 times more light,
but gives you 100 times

00:04:17.480 --> 00:04:20.321
better performance.

00:04:20.321 --> 00:04:21.940
Light is social.

00:04:21.940 --> 00:04:25.160
Light is life.

00:04:25.160 --> 00:04:29.410
This is about strength, and
about power, and about energy,

00:04:29.410 --> 00:04:33.440
about happiness and love, and
that's the same for everybody.

00:04:33.440 --> 00:04:34.730
This is energy for all.

00:04:34.730 --> 00:04:38.080
[MUSIC PLAYING]

